; Regression: a statement-position `if <set> else if <set>` chain with NO
; final else mis-emitted a DEAD `if.value` phi at the outer merge block.
; emit_if returned the no-else inner if's then-branch value as "the if's
; value"; that value (computed INSIDE the inner then-block) does not
; dominate the inner merge block, so the outer phi's incoming operand
; failed LLVM verification ("Instruction does not dominate all uses!").
; The in-process -o path at -O0 ran no verifier and executed correctly
; (the phi was dead), but --jit (ORC verifies) aborted and the external
; -S -> opt/llc archive path rejected the module. Fix: a no-else if
; yields NO value (emit_if returns null), so no merge phi is built.
; This test pins the SEMANTICS on the -o path (both arms + fall-through);
; the verifier regression is pinned by the literate JIT test
; controlflow.sgm if-else-if-no-else (tests/selfhosted).

function clamp(dmin: int) returns int
{
    var adj 7
    if dmin > 100
        set adj: 0
    else if dmin > 50
        set adj: dmin + 1
    adj
}

var ok true
if clamp(200) <> 0
    set ok: false
if clamp(60) <> 61
    set ok: false
if clamp(10) <> 7
    set ok: false

if ok
    print("PASS")
else
    print("FAIL")
